# Byte-compiled Python, created whenever the pipeline is imported
# rather than run. Nothing here belongs in the repo.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Local editor and assistant settings. Machine-specific, so they would only
# ever cause conflicts if they were shared. Two things are re-included: the
# launch config, the shared settings file and the hook it wires up, and this
# repository's own skills. settings.local.json stays ignored: that is Claude
# Code's per-machine file and it holds one person's permission allowlist,
# where settings.json is the checked-in one every session should agree on.
.claude/*
!.claude/launch.json
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/hooks/
!.claude/skills/
.claude/skills/*
!.claude/skills/juke-*/

# The prefix is what separates a skill written FOR Juke from one installed on
# this machine, and it has to, because `npx skills add` writes SYMLINKS into
# .claude/skills/ pointing at absolute paths under .agents/ — committing one
# would ship a path that exists on nobody else's disk. Nothing that command
# installs is named juke-*, so a skill named `juke-<something>` ships and
# anything else stays local. Name it right and it needs no line here.

# The same rule, for the tools that write somewhere other than .agents/.
# .codex/ is Codex's own hooks file and .github/skills/ is where Impeccable
# installs its skill bundle - 52 files and 17MB of third-party instruction
# files that run with full agent permissions, which is exactly what the
# paragraph below refuses for `npx skills add`. .impeccable/questions/ is
# per-run scratch, a log and a state file per question; the parts of
# .impeccable/ that are a shared record - config.json, critique/, surfaces/ -
# are tracked and stay tracked.
#
# These were sitting untracked in every `git status` on the shared checkout,
# which is worse than untidy here: this repository has already had one session
# sweep another's untracked files into a commit with `git add -A`, and a folder
# two dozen sessions share is the one place that matters most.
#
# .github/agents/ and .github/hooks/ are deliberately NOT here. They are small,
# readable and arguably belong to the project rather than to a machine - that
# is the owner's call to make, not one to settle by adding a line.
.codex/
.github/skills/
.impeccable/questions/

# Agent skills installed by `npx skills add`, and the lockfile pinning them.
# Third-party instruction files that run with full agent permissions, chosen
# per machine rather than per project — the same reasoning as .claude/ above,
# whose own skills/ directory is symlinks into here and is covered by the
# .claude/skills/* line above. The lockfile goes with them: it exists to
# reproduce an install,
# and there is nothing to reproduce once the skills are not shared.
.agents/
skills-lock.json

# The end-to-end test runner and what it leaves behind. The app itself has no
# dependencies and no build step — package.json exists only so `npm install`
# can fetch Playwright, and none of this is served, imported or needed to run
# the site. A checked-in node_modules would also be published, since Pages
# serves the whole repository.
node_modules/
test-results/
playwright-report/

# web/'s build output. Cloudflare Pages builds this itself on every deploy
# (Root directory: web, Build command: npm run build, Output directory:
# dist) — a checked-in copy would be yesterday's data behind a hashed
# filename nobody bumped.
web/dist/

# The intermediate Node-loadable SSR bundle scripts/prerender.mjs builds to
# render the homepage's initial HTML — consumed once during `npm run build`
# and thrown away, not an artifact of anything.
web/dist-ssr/

# wrangler's local state: the Durable Object storage it fakes for
# `wrangler dev`, its bundle cache and its temp files. 18MB of machine-local
# scratch that is rebuilt on demand, and a checked-in copy would be someone
# else's half-finished draft.
#
# Both paths, because there are two ways to start it and they do not agree.
# wrangler writes this beside the CURRENT DIRECTORY rather than beside the
# config it was handed, so CLAUDE.md's `cd worker && wrangler dev` puts it in
# worker/ while playwright.config.mjs's `wrangler dev -c worker/wrangler.toml`
# runs from the repo root and puts it here. Only the first was ignored, so a
# root .wrangler/ has been sitting untracked in `git status` after every suite
# run — and this repository has already had one session sweep another's
# untracked files into a commit with `git add -A`. Noise in `git status` is
# what makes that easy to do.
worker/.wrangler/
.wrangler/

# Local secrets for `wrangler dev`. The two proxied routes need a key and the
# keys live in the worker, never in the page — so testing them locally means
# putting real ones in a file next to wrangler.toml. There are no secrets in
# this repository and there must not be.
worker/.dev.vars

# Clerk's publishable key is public by design (see web/src/clerkConfig.js),
# but a local .env is still where a contributor's own dev-instance key lives
# — web/.env.example documents the variable name without a real value.
web/.env
web/.env.local

# Folder metadata the operating system writes on its own. This repository
# lives inside OneDrive, which drops a desktop.ini in any folder it has
# been given an icon or a localised name for — so it reappears on its own
# after every delete. Nothing to do with the site, and Pages serves the
# whole repository, so a stray one would be published at jukeff.com.
desktop.ini
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
